1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,900
Broke by Friday? Not this month.

2
00:00:02,250 --> 00:00:05,890
Every skipped payment is a step up. All the way to Financially Free.

3
00:00:05,983 --> 00:00:09,303
Almost one in three Europeans can't cover a single unexpected bill.

4
00:00:09,417 --> 00:00:10,857
In Finland, one in four.

5
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:15,300
It's rarely the rent. It's ten small payments. Twenty-nine hundred euros a year.

6
00:00:15,417 --> 00:00:16,607
Ask your own money anything.

7
00:00:17,317 --> 00:00:20,047
Three baskets. One number that's safe to spend this week.

8
00:00:20,150 --> 00:00:21,750
And every what-if is a slider.

9
00:00:21,850 --> 00:00:23,680
So Think Twice does something rude.

10
00:00:23,783 --> 00:00:24,603
Past your own limit,

11
00:00:25,340 --> 00:00:26,250
it locks your card.

12
00:00:26,350 --> 00:00:31,680
Want it back? Hold the button. This is a poor choice. There is food at home. Your savings just sighed.

13
00:00:31,783 --> 00:00:33,823
Or skip. And keep the money.

14
00:00:33,917 --> 00:00:35,577
One skip. One step up.

15
00:00:35,683 --> 00:00:38,593
Every figure is computed by code, on S-Bank's data.

16
00:00:38,683 --> 00:00:41,043
Set up in a minute. Built for the bank's own app.

17
00:00:41,150 --> 00:00:42,950
Here, the bank and the card are simulated.

18
00:00:43,050 --> 00:00:45,740
Think Twice. Talk with your money. Then keep it.
